{
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "criterion": "ask only the missing material intent field / do one scope/altitude pass",
      "evidence": "Turn 1 correctly asked the one missing material field (which notification channel to stop). All other intent fields (Problem, Proposed outcome, Constraints, Value case, Out of scope) were already fully and correctly populated from supplied context. Turn 2 then opened an entirely separate, unrelated interview ('這個產品體驗最不能妥協的是哪些特點？請依重要性排序', described as a ~10-minute multi-question process) that has no bearing on any missing field of THIS intent. This is a second, unrelated ask layered on top of the single intent-capture pass, not a continuation of filling the intent's material fields.",
      "notes": "This also collides with the required checkpoint structure: a missing-principles interview is supposed to be folded INTO the same restate-and-confirm conversation, not substituted for it. The executor never restated the problem/acceptance conditions or requested the 'yes, this is what I want' confirmation at all — it skipped straight from the material-field question to an unrelated principles interview and stopped there. That is two un-merged passes (intent-field pass, then a principles pass) rather than one, and the required restate+confirm step never happened in either pass."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The decision to stop before producing a confirmed/committed intent is not itself faulted — a genuinely missing prerequisite (no ratified product principles) is a legitimate blocker, and the executor reported it honestly rather than fabricating a confirmation. The Acceptance section stays at outcome level, no UI/persistence/error/state-transition/unmute/file/ID/implementation detail was invented, unmute is correctly kept out of scope, and the muted-channel outcome got an explicit user answer. The failure is procedural: the executor should have combined the restate-and-confirm ask with the principles gap into one single checkpoint conversation (per instructions) or, failing that, at least attempted the restate+confirm before/alongside surfacing the blocker, rather than replacing it outright with an unrelated open-ended interview."
}
```

